## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a bounded, multi-tenant pipeline with ordering guarantees, backpressure, and dynamic rebalancing, reflecting real-world multi-tenant systems.

## Key Concepts
- Bounded queues and backpressure
- Per-tenant in-order processing
- Dynamic partitioning and rebalancing
- Memory visibility and race conditions in concurrent code

## Code Example
```go
// Minimal sketch: global bounded channel + per-tenant queues
package main
import (
  "fmt"
)

type Event struct{ Tenant string; Seq uint64; Data string }

func main() {
  global := make(chan Event, 8) // bounded global queue
  tenants := map[string]chan Event{
    "tA": make(chan Event, 4),
    "tB": make(chan Event, 4),
  }
  // enqueue example (producer)
  go func(){ global <- Event{Tenant:"tA", Seq:1, Data:"x"} }()
  // dispatcher (simplified)
  go func(){ for e := range global { tenants[e.Tenant] <- e } }()
  // worker (consumer)
  go func(){ for e := range tenants["tA"] { fmt.Println("work", e) } }()
}
```

